{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789863588,"nonce":"85gkcyxqo0Ysny1T/8yoWhZm/EE=","title":"Every compound statement forgot which variables were known to be instances","message":"The lowering knows a Class-typed variable is not None once it was checked or assigned a constructor's result, and skips the None check on its next attribute access. It cleared that knowledge before and after every if, while, for, try, with and match, so a method reading self.x, an if, then x.y checked x again, and a `while t is not None` body checked t at every access: richards' HandlerTask.fn had 9 checks for 12 reads before the optimiser folded the dominated ones.\n\nA compound statement now drops only the variables it assigns (a try or match, or one with a nested body, still drops all), and a while body starts with what its test settled.","files":null}]}